==Strategy==
==='''Chapter 1'''===
With enough [[Anti-Starred Alien Treasures]], this should be a rather easy Outbreak. Just be sure to bring [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and at least one [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|Critical Hitter]] to deal with the Metal enemies, as the Cat Deploy Limit of 5 makes chipping them down without a Critter really annoying and tedious.

==='''Chapter 2'''===
Try focusing on stallers rather than numbers here, as using [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] and [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|King Dragon Cat]] to outrange most enemies in the stage if you want to, can lead to an easy victory.

==='''Chapter 3'''===
You can rush this stage with a combination of rapidly attacking critters, like [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Cat Researcher]] and [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Hurricat]], alongside [[Talents|Talented]] [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Awakened Bahamut Cat]]. Bring [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]] to help with consistency.

First, spawn Hurricat to take care of the initial Metal Doge, and let him die to Shibalien Elite. Kill Zoge and Shibalien with Bahamut, then stall Metal Hippoe with [[Crazed Tank Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Manic Eraser Cats]], ensuring that Bahamut isn't juggled to death. Kill Zoge when he revives with [[Teacher BearCat (Rare Cat)|Cadaver BearCat]], and finally go on the offensive with Hurricats and Cat Researches to swarm the horde of Metals that appear on base hit, all to clear the stage in record time. Deathshund will burrow beneath everybody, and your critters + Bahamut will take care of the frontlines. This strategy can be a bit dicey, but you only need one lucky break to pull it off.

